# Copy to /etc/uptime-watch/targets. One check per line: type name target [comment]
# Types:
#   http   URL        page answers 2xx or 3xx
#   render URL        like http, plus the x-render-origin-server header (app is served by Render)
#   cert   host       TLS certificate valid for at least CERT_MIN_DAYS days
#   dnscf  host       all A records (via 1.1.1.1) are Cloudflare addresses (proxied)
#   mx     domain=host  this host is in the domain's MX records
#   tcp    host:port  port is open
# name is used for the state file, so keep it unique and without spaces.
# type    name        target
http      site        https://example.com/
http      site-www    https://www.example.com/
render    app-login   https://example.com/login
cert      cert-apex   example.com
cert      cert-www    www.example.com
dnscf     dns-apex    example.com
dnscf     dns-www     www.example.com
mx        dns-mx      example.com=mx1.example.com
tcp       ssh         example.com:22
